     "result_text_tail": "w numbering, and marked the end-page owners \"(proposed)\" as the analysis does.\n\n**Numbers that come only from the analysis**\nThese six aren't in the briefing pack; they're sourced to the analysis and listed as unverified:\n- 50 shipping weeks a year, used to size the buffer stock;\n- a 25% annual inventory carrying cost;\n- about 25% of volume going to the alternate shop;\n- $2 freight on top of the $88 emergency price;\n- buffer stock being available immediately;\n- deciding on an owned cell at least 12 months before the capacity is needed.\n\nThe last one sits in a gate. Since you weren't available, I kept it as the analysis's figure and flagged it.\n\n**Choices I made for you**\n- I used the navy theme.\n- I made the summary's headline the recommendation itself, kept short enough to fit on one line: \"Keep buying in 2027 on a de-risked supply, pre-qualify a gated lease, and build no cell in 2027\".\n\n**Remaining QA warnings (none affect the content)**\n- Several slides are denser than the skill's guideline, because the analysis is dense and the rules say not to drop content.\n- Four titles run 22\u201323 words, though all fit on two lines.\n- On the five-layer contingency slide, $0.25M and $0.72M are written as text in the table: the tool would otherwise round them to \"$0.2M\" and \"$0.7M\".\n\nNo \"?\" placeholders remain. I couldn't open the slides as images here, so please flip through the deck before circulating it. The spec and build scripts are in `./work/` if you want to switch theme or rebuild."
